    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0209" n="1667" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p2/pg1667"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">110.11/5–1451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hong Kong</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hong Kong</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-05-14T11:00:00+09:00">May 14, 1951—11 a.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3369. To Acheson for Dep Under Secy Matthews,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d86-f1"/>
                    Marshall and Chase have made available of all known possible contacts. They plan
                    wait till May 19. Thereupon if nothing to justify their continuation here has
                    appeared they will return to Washington. Meantime they request any further
                    instructions or relevant info from you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d86-f1" n="1" xml:id="d86-f1-content">
                <p>The telegram was circulated to Frederick E. Nolting, Special Assistant to the
                    Deputy Under Secretary; Nitze; and Merchant.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
